240
00:14:19,520 --> 00:14:23,873
The books of Ohara must be kept out
of the government's hands at any cost.

241
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:31,150
Still.

242
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:34,776
I could not resist making
the trip to Elbaf in secret.

243
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:41,800
I read every last document there.

244
00:14:42,340 --> 00:14:49,240
And now, the mystery that Ohara
unraveled lives on in my brain.

245
00:14:50,140 --> 00:14:53,846
I've been continuing their research
in secret to this very day.

246
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:56,200
Vegapunk, I have a question.

247
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:59,520
That strange giant you mentioned.

248
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:09,260
It's Sol, isn't it?

249
00:15:12,220 --> 00:15:13,480
He's in hiding now.

250
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:16,864
No one else can know the truth.

251
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:27,060
Thank you, Dr. Vegapunk.

252
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:29,457
You've kept the dream of Ahura alive.

253
00:15:29,540 --> 00:15:30,880
I can never repay you.

254
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:34,837
You need not thank me for pursuing
all branches of knowledge.

255
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:36,626
That is the way of a scholar.

256
00:15:48,300 --> 00:15:52,000
Where are these crazy
future shoes taking me?

257
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:58,624
I'm afraid I can't release you.

258
00:15:58,840 --> 00:15:59,980
But do come along.

259
00:16:00,780 --> 00:16:02,898
There's something I need you to see.

260
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:06,140
It really hid this robot's cockpit, huh?

261
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:08,740
Wait a sec.

262
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:10,877
What if the robot doesn't need one?

263
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:12,600
What if it's self-piloting?

264
00:16:13,080 --> 00:16:14,580
Let's try talking to it.

265
00:16:14,760 --> 00:16:15,819
It might activate.

266
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:18,220
Okay, let's see.

267
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:20,800
Robot, get up and go!

268
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:23,220
Aw, nope.

269
00:16:23,680 --> 00:16:26,120
Wonder if there's a password. No way.

270
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:27,654
We just need its name.

271
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:29,120
I'll guess it easy.

272
00:16:30,680 --> 00:16:32,220
Wake up, Root-gobberts!

273
00:16:35,140 --> 00:16:35,970
Rubinovsky!

274
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:37,400
Come on.

275
00:16:37,780 --> 00:16:39,251
What are you, like, five?

276
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:42,028
This thing doesn't work
like a freaking toy.

277
00:16:50,780 --> 00:16:52,060
No way!

278
00:17:02,380 --> 00:17:04,040
Is everyone all right?

279
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:05,260
I'm fine.

280
00:17:05,520 --> 00:17:06,420
Oh, no.

281
00:17:06,640 --> 00:17:08,169
Robobber, did you explode?

282
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:10,680
No, that wasn't an explosion.

283
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:13,359
But then, what in the world was it?

284
00:17:15,020 --> 00:17:15,850
Help!

285
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:19,920
I request a help!

286
00:17:21,220 --> 00:17:23,820
Wait, Quasar? Oh, Zounds!

287
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:25,866
I've made a terrible mistake.

288
00:17:26,060 --> 00:17:27,840
I request a help, please.

289
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:31,540
It's best time to start
while I was wopping?

290
00:17:32,020 --> 00:17:33,785
Was that old man there before?

291
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:35,480
I don't think so, no.

292
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:36,530
I am thinking!

293
00:17:36,613 --> 00:17:38,540
Thinking like a fresh egg!

294
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:40,420
But you made to die!

295
00:17:43,460 --> 00:17:45,519
I don't really get what's going on.

296
00:17:45,880 --> 00:17:48,115
Okay, old man, I'll see what I can do!

297
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:56,617
Please, my dear boy, get
me out of here! Wait a sec.

298
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:59,360
This is just like when I met Keenumon.

299
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:03,460
Quickly now, quickly!

300
00:18:07,060 --> 00:18:08,940
It really is there!

301
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:16,180
I thought so. It's him!

302
00:18:18,520 --> 00:18:19,620
Thank you.

303
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:21,520
Your dragon-son, I believe.

304
00:18:22,060 --> 00:18:24,240
I heard that you arrived here.

305
00:18:24,420 --> 00:18:25,657
You and your friends.

306
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:28,340
And you are Bonnie!

307
00:18:29,100 --> 00:18:31,900
You're all grown up! Dr. Vegapunk!

308
00:18:32,520 --> 00:18:34,660
And the picture of him!

309
00:18:35,620 --> 00:18:37,680
Old man, can you fly?

310
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:39,960
You can too with those boots!

311
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:43,160
Your dom shoes are just like mine.

312
00:18:43,420 --> 00:18:45,500
They have a hover function. Really?

313
00:18:45,740 --> 00:18:46,960
How do we use it?

314
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:51,489
First, press the little
button on the side.

315
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:54,170
Found it!

316
00:18:54,253 --> 00:18:59,340
And next, take this lever
and push it down. Like so!

317
00:19:01,280 --> 00:19:02,520
Very good!

318
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:11,180
It's so too high!

319
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:17,580
I need faith, Marcus!

320
00:20:24,180 --> 00:20:29,220
I'll just hold you one more time.

321
00:20:30,720 --> 00:20:36,620
I'm laughing at you.

322
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:41,580
I'm going to sing along the same song.

323
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:45,860
Even if you're a teenager,

324
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:49,140
I don't want to forget.
